{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And he saw the Kenite, etc.</b> This is Jethro, and the intent of the verse follows what they of blessed memory said (Bava Batra 15a): 'Eitan' — this is Abraham, and Abraham was the first righteous convert, and all converts are called by the name Abraham. And they of blessed memory said (Shemot Rabbah 27:6) that Jethro converted. Therefore he said <b>your dwelling-place is eitan</b>, meaning your dwelling-place corresponds to Abraham, who was called eitan. And his saying <b>and set in the rock</b>, etc., means: furthermore, you have placed your ken (nest) in the rock — meaning your ken is the daughter you gave to Moses, and Moses was traced to the rock (sela) because he was mighty in Torah and in the strength of kingship. Also, sela alludes to Torah as stated in the book of Zohar (Tikkunei Zohar 21), and Moses was called by its name."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The comment interprets the verse's word אֵיתָן ('eitan,' 'firm/enduring') by linking it to Abraham via the rabbinic identification in Bava Batra 15a. The wordplay on קֵן ('ken,' 'nest') and the name קֵינִי ('Kenite') is rendered by preserving 'ken' in transliteration."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:14:03.994442044Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}